    "@type": "xsd:date",
    "@value": "1937-08-04"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/dust-bowl/timeline/11",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "With near-normal rain returning from 1938, the drought ends.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYear",
    "@value": "1940"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/dust-bowl/timeline/2",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "Drought ruins the Southern Plains wheat crop in the autumn, leaving fields bare.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYear",
    "@value": "1931"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/dust-bowl/timeline/3",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "By late January winds are lifting loose soil into dust storms.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYearMonth",
    "@value": "1932-01"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/dust-bowl/timeline/4",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "The Soil Erosion Service is set up in the Interior Department with Hugh Hammond Bennett as chief.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYearMonth",
    "@value": "1933-09"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/dust-bowl/timeline/5",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "A great dust storm carries Plains soil over Washington, D.C., and out over the Atlantic.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:date",
    "@value": "1934-05-11"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/dust-bowl/timeline/6",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "A second March dust cloud darkens Washington as Congress holds hearings on soil conservation.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:date",
    "@value": "1935-03-21"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/dust-bowl/timeline/7",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "Black Sunday: a dust front sweeps from central Nebraska toward the Mexican border; a reporter's account names the Dust Bowl.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:date",
    "@value": "1935-04-14"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/dust-bowl/timeline/8",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "Roosevelt signs the Soil Conservation Act, creating the permanent Soil Conservation Service in the Agriculture Department.",
   "uso:date": {
