    "@value": "1844"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/harriet-tubman/timeline/3",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "After her enslaver Edward Brodess dies in March, she fears being sold, escapes alone in the late fall and reaches Philadelphia.",
   "uso:date": {
    "@type": "xsd:gYear",
    "@value": "1849"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/harriet-tubman/timeline/4",
   "@type": "uso:TimelineEntry",
   "rdfs:label": "Congress passes the Fugitive Slave Act; Tubman makes her first rescue, of her niece Kessiah and Kessiah's two children.",
