   "skos:definition": "The mass migration to California set off when James Marshall found gold at John Sutter's sawmill on the American River on January 24, 1848; it drew some 300,000 people from across the world by the mid-1850s, sped California to statehood as a free state in 1850, enriched merchants more than most miners, and brought dispossession, forced labor and mass death to Native Californians and discriminatory taxes on foreign miners.",
