    }
   ],
   "skos:definition": "The 1831 U.S. Supreme Court case in which the Cherokee Nation asked the Court to stop Georgia from enforcing its laws on Cherokee land; the Court dismissed the suit for lack of jurisdiction, holding that the Nation was not a foreign state under Article III but one of the \"domestic dependent nations\" whose relation to the United States resembled that of a ward to a guardian.",
