   },
   "skos:definition": "The Latin motto \"E pluribus unum\" (\"Out of many, one\"), first proposed for a national seal in August 1776 and adopted on the Great Seal of the United States in 1782, where it refers to the union of the states; federal law still requires it on U.S. coins, though it was never designated the national motto.",
