   },
   "skos:definition": "The 1868 amendment to the U.S. Constitution that made all persons born or naturalized in the United States citizens and barred states from denying any person due process of law or the equal protection of the laws; it also reshaped representation, barred certain former officials who joined the rebellion from office, and settled Civil War debts.",
