   "skos:definition": "A wave of strikes, protests and riots that began on the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad at Martinsburg, West Virginia, on July 16, 1877, spread along the rail lines from Baltimore to Chicago and St. Louis, and was put down by state militias and federal troops, leaving about a hundred people dead.",
