   "skos:definition": "A freedom seeker, Underground Railroad conductor, Union scout and nurse, and women's-suffrage advocate (c. 1822–1913) who escaped slavery in Maryland in 1849, returned about 13 times to lead roughly 70 family members and friends to freedom, and helped lead the 1863 Combahee River raid that freed more than 700 enslaved people.",
