   "skos:definition": "The fiftieth U.S. state (admitted August 21, 1959), a volcanic island chain in the north Pacific settled by Polynesian voyagers centuries before European contact; an independent Native Hawaiian kingdom until a U.S.-backed overthrow in 1893, it was annexed by joint resolution in 1898 over petitions signed by more than half of Native Hawaiians and governed as a territory until statehood.",
