   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "us:indian-removal"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The federal law signed by President Andrew Jackson on May 28, 1830, that authorized the president to exchange lands west of the Mississippi River for the homelands of Native nations in the East, and that became the legal basis for the forced removal of the Cherokee, Muscogee (Creek), Choctaw, Chickasaw, Seminole and other nations in the 1830s and 1840s.",
