    "Long Depression"
   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "us:economic-history-of-the-united-states"
   },
   "skos:definition": "A financial crisis that began when the railroad-financing bank Jay Cooke and Company failed on September 18, 1873, closed the New York Stock Exchange for ten days, and set off a depression that lasted until about 1879, ruining thousands of businesses, sinking the Freedman's Savings Bank and helping to turn national politics away from Reconstruction.",
