   "skos:definition": "An abolitionist, preacher and women's-rights advocate (c. 1797–1883) who was born enslaved in Ulster County, New York, freed herself in 1826, won a New York court case in 1828 to recover her son from slavery in Alabama, and from 1843 travelled as Sojourner Truth, speaking against slavery and for the rights of women and freed people.",
