   },
   "skos:definition": "A federal republic in North America made up of fifty states and the District of Columbia, with five inhabited territories and 575 federally recognized tribal nations within its borders; it declared independence from Great Britain on July 4, 1776, took its name in 1776, won recognition in the Treaty of Paris of 1783, and has been governed under the Constitution since 1789.",
