   "skos:definition": "A pair of 30-foot bronze winged figures by the Norwegian-born sculptor Oskar J. W. Hansen, set on black diorite bases beside a 142-foot flagpole in a terrazzo plaza on the Nevada end of Hoover Dam, whose inlaid star map fixes the sky at the moment Franklin D. Roosevelt dedicated the dam on September 30, 1935.",
