     "@id": "us:voting-rights-in-the-united-states"
    },
    {
     "@id": "us:womens-rights-movement"
    }
   ],
   "skos:definition": "The seven-decade campaign to win American women the right to vote, which began with the women's rights conventions of the late 1840s, split and reunited over the Reconstruction amendments, won the vote state by state in the West, and secured the Nineteenth Amendment in 1920, though many women of color stayed disfranchised for decades afterward.",
