   "skos:definition": "The first national park in the United States, set aside by an act of Congress signed by President Ulysses S. Grant on March 1, 1872; it covers about 2.2 million acres, mostly in northwestern Wyoming with slivers in Montana and Idaho, protects more than 10,000 hydrothermal features atop an active volcanic caldera, and lies on lands that 27 Native nations have used for more than 11,000 years.",
